<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    Radio-side degradation of the active leg (see [Config UplinkBadRadio] in
    omnetpp_uplink.ini).

    Simu5G's channel model caches every one of its parameters into C++ members
    at initialize() (LteRealisticChannelModel.cc:47-92), so ScenarioManager's
    <set-param> cannot touch shadowing, fading, scenario, noise figures, tx
    power or anything else about the channel once the run has started. The one
    input that *is* re-read on every transmission is the node position:
    LteRealisticChannelModel::getAttenuation() calls phy_->getCoord() per
    computation (LteRealisticChannelModel.cc:106).

    So geometry is the runtime knob for radio quality, and the way to drive it
    on a schedule is a scripted mobility model. TurtleMobility takes exactly
    this kind of timeline.

    Timeline: ue[0] sits at its nominal spot until t=2s, then covers the
    distance in 1s and stays put for the remaining 2s of the run. Path loss
    climbs, CQI reports collapse, the uplink grants shrink, HARQ
    retransmissions pile up, and both latency and loss go up on the leg that
    actually carries the traffic.

    The 1s transit is deliberately faster than anything physical; the point
    is to spend most of the run in the degraded state, not to model a walk.
    Stretch it if you want to watch the quality decay gradually instead.
-->
<movements>
    <movement id="walkAway">
        <!-- Same coordinates as *.ue[0].mobility.initialX/Y in the ini: with
             initFromDisplayString off and no initialX parameter on
             TurtleMobility, the script is what fixes the starting point. -->
        <!-- No speed here: TurtleMobility rejects speed="0" outright, and
             <wait> holds the position regardless of what speed says. -->
        <set x="950" y="250"/>
        <wait t="2"/>

        <!-- 2D distance to the gNB at (750,350) goes 224m -> 1852m, i.e. about
             34dB of extra UMi NLOS path loss at 3.5GHz. Measured effect on the
             class-6 stream: 4298 of 4500 packets delivered without this script,
             2846 with it. Pull the endpoint back in for a milder leg; 2000m of
             2D distance is the hard ceiling before NrChannelModel throws
             (NrChannelModel.cc, computeUrbanMicro). -->
        <moveto x="2550" y="250" t="1"/>

        <!-- Park there for the rest of the run. -->
        <wait t="100"/>
    </movement>
</movements>
